          <p class="kicker">Supported platforms for analytics</p>
          <h2>Platform coverage</h2>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p class="intro">Before comparing metrics, the first question is simple: does the tool report analytics for the networks you actually use? Publishing support and analytics support are not the same thing — a tool can let you schedule a post to a network without ever telling you how that post performed. The table below is scoped specifically to analytics: which networks each tool actually reports on, not just which ones it can post to.</p><p class="intro">Zoho Social covers the widest range here — eleven networks with analytics, including two that none of the other three touch at all: Google My Business and Mastodon. It's also the only tool in this comparison that reports analytics for LinkedIn personal profiles in addition to LinkedIn company pages. Buffer sits at the opposite end, with analytics limited to four networks — X, Instagram, Facebook, and LinkedIn — even though it can publish more broadly. Sprout Social and Hootsuite land in between, each missing a handful of networks the others cover (Sprout has no Mastodon or GMB; Hootsuite has no Bluesky, Mastodon, GMB, or Reddit).</p>
      
