      <div class="analysis"><p class="analysis-label">Reading the data</p><p class="analysis-p">A pattern worth flagging: every tool draws the line in a slightly different place on the “newer” or smaller networks. Bluesky is supported by Zoho Social and Sprout Social, but not Hootsuite. Threads and TikTok are covered by everyone except Buffer. Reddit is Sprout Social's one exclusive — none of the other three report on it at all. None of the four tools support WhatsApp or Telegram analytics, which lines up with those platforms' more restrictive developer APIs for business messaging data.</p><p class="analysis-p">Free-plan access compounds these gaps. Even where a network is technically supported, the free or entry tier often caps how many total channels can be connected before analytics becomes relevant at all — Zoho Social allows 6 connected channels on its Free plan (5 of which carry analytics), Sprout Social's Standard plan allows 5, and Hootsuite's Standard plan allows 10. Sprout Social and Hootsuite, notably, don't have a permanent free plan in the first place — see Section 12 for how that plays out.</p></div>
      
      
