    <section class="section" id="post-metrics">
      <div class="section-head">
        <span class="section-num">02</span>
        <div>
          <p class="kicker">Facebook · Instagram · LinkedIn · X (Twitter)</p>
          <h2>Post performance metrics</h2>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p class="intro">Platform coverage answers “which networks.” Post metrics answer the more important question: what does the tool actually tell you about how a piece of content performed? All four tools cover the basics — reactions, comments, shares, likes, engagement rate — on every network. The differences show up in the metrics that reveal true content reach: viral impressions, unique impressions, engaged fans on Facebook; reach and repost data on LinkedIn and X; and how much of a Reel or Story gets measured on Instagram.</p>
