    <section class="section" id="demographics">
      <div class="section-head">
        <span class="section-num">03</span>
        <div>
          <p class="kicker">Know exactly who you're reaching</p>
          <h2>Audience demographics</h2>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p class="intro">This section is about whether a platform tells you *who* your audience is — age, gender, location, job title, seniority, industry — not how many followers you have or how fast that number is growing. Follower growth is a headcount metric; demographics is a composition metric. The two get conflated often enough that it's worth stating plainly: a tool can report follower growth without ever telling you whether those new followers are the people you're trying to reach.</p><p class="intro">The first row in the table below combines platform coverage with each tool's deepest available breakdown in one line; the rows underneath it go network by network so you can see exactly what each platform exposes.</p>
      
    <div class="table-block">
      
      <div class="table-wrap">
        <table>
          <thead><tr><th>Feature</th><th>Zoho Social</th><th>Buffer</th><th>Sprout Social</th><th>Hootsuite</th></tr></thead>
          <tbody><tr><td class="col-label"><span class="cell-label">Platforms with audience demographics &amp; deepest breakdown</span></td><td>IG, LinkedIn, YouTube — deepest on LinkedIn (industry, job function, seniority, company size)</td><td>IG only (fully), FB (location only) — deepest on Instagram (age, gender, cities, countries)</td><td>FB (age, gender, country, city), IG, LinkedIn (seniority, job function), YouTube — deepest on LinkedIn (seniority, job function standard; industry, company size need connected profiles)</td><td>FB, IG, LinkedIn, TikTok, X, YouTube — deepest on LinkedIn (seniority, job function, industry, B2B segmentation, where data sources allow)</td></tr><tr><td class="col-label"><span class="cell-label">LinkedIn audience demographics</span></td><td><span class="stat stat-yes"><i class="dot"></i>Yes</span><span class="cell-rest">seniority, job function, industry, company size, experience level, location</span></td><td><span class="stat stat-no"><i class="dot"></i>Not available</span></td><td><span class="stat stat-yes"><i class="dot"></i>Yes</span><span class="cell-rest">by seniority level, audience top job functions</span></td><td><span class="stat stat-yes"><i class="dot"></i>Yes</span></td></tr><tr><td class="col-label"><span class="cell-label">Facebook audience demographics</span></td><td><span class="stat stat-partial"><i class="dot"></i>Deprecated</span><span class="cell-rest">Nov 15, 2025 — follower count only now</span></td><td>Location only (age/gender removed via Meta API)</td><td><span class="stat stat-yes"><i class="dot"></i>Yes</span><span class="cell-rest">by age, gender, country, city (delayed 48–72 hours; requires 100+ data points per segment)</span></td><td><span class="stat stat-partial"><i class="dot"></i>Limited</span><span class="cell-rest">Meta API restrictions apply</span></td></tr><tr><td class="col-label"><span class="cell-label">Instagram audience demographics</span></td><td>Age, gender, country, language</td><td>Age, gender, top cities, countries</td><td><span class="stat stat-yes"><i class="dot"></i>Yes</span><span class="cell-rest">age, gender, location (Demographics tab in Instagram Business Profiles Report); minimum 100 followers required before age and gender are displayed</span></td><td><span class="stat stat-yes"><i class="dot"></i>Yes</span><span class="cell-rest">age, gender, location</span></td></tr><tr><td class="col-label"><span class="cell-label">YouTube subscriber demographics</span></td><td>Only subscribers by geography available.</td><td><span class="stat stat-no"><i class="dot"></i>No</span></td><td><span class="stat stat-yes"><i class="dot"></i>Yes</span><span class="cell-rest">YouTube reporting features available</span></td><td><span class="stat stat-yes"><i class="dot"></i>Yes</span><span class="cell-rest">subscriber and audience analytics available through YouTube Analytics integration.</span></td></tr></tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
      
    </div>
    
      
      <div class="analysis"><p class="analysis-label">Reading the data</p><p class="analysis-p">LinkedIn is consistently the deepest demographic breakdown across all four tools — and for good reason: it's the one network built around professional identity, so seniority, job function, industry, and company size are native to the data LinkedIn exposes. Zoho Social's LinkedIn breakdown is the most complete of the four on paper (adding experience level and location to the standard seniority/job-function pair), though Hootsuite covers the widest span of networks overall — six, versus Zoho Social's three (Facebook, Instagram, LinkedIn) if YouTube's geography-only data is set aside as partial.</p><p class="analysis-p">Instagram demographics carry a hidden gate worth flagging for planning purposes: Sprout Social requires a minimum of 100 followers on the connected account before it will display age and gender data at all. A newly connected or small account will simply show no demographic breakdown until it crosses that threshold — worth knowing before assuming the feature is broken rather than gated.</p></div>
      <div class="callout"><p>Meta deprecated Facebook age and gender audience data on November 15, 2025. All four tools now show follower count and location only for Facebook — this is a platform-side API change that affects every tool equally, not a gap specific to any one of them.</p></div>
      
