      <div class="analysis"><p class="analysis-label">Reading the data</p><p class="analysis-p">Zoho Social and Hootsuite are the only two tools here offering a genuine drag-and-drop dashboard builder without an add-on — Sprout Social's equivalent customization sits behind Premium Analytics, and Buffer offers no dashboard builder at all. Mobile is a weaker spot for Zoho Social specifically: the mobile app surfaces individual post stats but not the analytics tab itself, while Sprout Social's and Hootsuite's mobile apps both carry fuller reporting.</p><p class="analysis-p">On sorting and filtering, the pattern across Sprout Social is consistent with what shows up elsewhere in this comparison: the base plan covers standard sorting and filtering, but anything described as “custom” — custom metric sorting, internal tag filtering — requires the separate Premium Analytics add-on. Buffer's cross-channel post overview is capped at a fixed 7-day Home view with no way to extend the range, which limits how useful it is for anything beyond a quick weekly check-in.</p></div>
      
      
