      <div class="analysis"><p class="analysis-label">Reading the data</p><p class="analysis-p">The retention windows on X and Facebook are worth noting for anyone building historical trend reports: Buffer stops updating Facebook post metrics after a calendar month and X metrics after just 20 days, which is the tightest cutoff of the four. Zoho Social's own window is also time-boxed — 30 posts for Facebook, 100 posts from the last 30 days for X — meaning older posts drop out of active reporting even though they remain published.</p><p class="analysis-p">On export, the one feature no tool offers on its entry tier is scheduled, automated report delivery — Zoho Social requires Premium or Agency, Sprout requires a premium plan, and Hootsuite gates it in ways that still exclude post-performance metrics specifically. Buffer doesn't offer scheduled delivery at any tier. If a recurring stakeholder report is part of the workflow, that's a real plan-tier decision point, not a checkbox difference.</p></div>
      
      
