    <section class="section" id="sentiment">
      <div class="section-head">
        <span class="section-num">07</span>
        <div>
          <p class="kicker">What people are saying, and how they feel about it</p>
          <h2>Sentiment analysis</h2>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p class="intro">Sentiment analysis automatically classifies mentions, comments, and messages about a brand as positive, negative, or neutral, so a team can gauge overall brand perception without reading every comment by hand. It's a different question from social listening (Section 08) — listening is about *finding* the conversation; sentiment is about *scoring the tone* of what you find.</p><p class="intro">Marketing pages for Zoho Social describe a sentiment analysis capability, but it was not found as a distinct, labelled feature inside the product's Monitor tab or Reports tab during a direct in-account check. That check is documented in the callout below rather than folded quietly into the table, because it changes how much weight the “Yes” claims for Zoho Social in this section should carry.</p>
      
