    <section class="section" id="listening">
      <div class="section-head">
        <span class="section-num">08</span>
        <div>
          <p class="kicker">Note: for Sprout Social, this is entirely an add-on feature</p>
          <h2>Social listening</h2>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p class="intro">Social listening tracks the broader conversation around a brand, keyword, or competitor across the open social web — not just the accounts you own. It's the discovery layer that feeds sentiment analysis (Section 07): listening finds the mentions, sentiment scores their tone. Sprout Social gates almost all listening capability behind a separate paid add-on; Hootsuite includes basic listening on every plan and reserves its deeper Talkwalker layer for enterprise; Buffer has none at all.</p>
      
