      <div class="analysis"><p class="analysis-label">Reading the data</p><p class="analysis-p">The biggest structural difference in this table isn't a feature gap — it's a pricing-model difference. Zoho Social bundles real-time mention monitoring, keyword/hashtag columns, and competitor tracking directly into its Monitor tab, no separate purchase required. Sprout Social offers a comparable feature set on paper, but almost every row requires its Listening add-on on top of a paid plan — meaning the sticker price of Sprout understates what full listening actually costs. Hootsuite splits the difference: Listening Basics ships free on every plan, but the wide-coverage Talkwalker layer (13+ networks, 30+ news and forum sources) is reserved for enterprise customers.</p><p class="analysis-p">Zoho Social's native Google Business reviews and questions monitoring is worth flagging on its own: Sprout Social doesn't include GMB in its Listening network list at all, and Hootsuite only added GMB review monitoring to its Inbox as of April 2026. For any brand that treats Google Business reviews as part of its reputation-management workflow, that's a meaningfully different starting point across the three tools.</p></div>
      
      
