      <div class="analysis"><p class="analysis-label">Reading the data</p><p class="analysis-p">The one row where Zoho Social is a clear “No” is formal benchmarking against competitors — the kind of structured report that puts your engagement, audience growth, and top posts side by side with a rival's. Sprout and Hootsuite both build this as a named, dedicated report (Competitor Reports; competitive benchmarking with industry comparisons), while Zoho Social's strength here is upstream of that: monitoring and tracking competitor activity, without following their profile, on the free-of-add-on Monitor tab. For a team that needs a presentation-ready side-by-side benchmark, Sprout or Hootsuite currently cover that specific need more completely than Zoho Social does.</p></div>
      
      
