    <section class="section" id="best-time">
      <div class="section-head">
        <span class="section-num">11</span>
        <div>
          <p class="kicker">When to publish — and how many times a day</p>
          <h2>Best time to post</h2>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p class="intro">“Best time to post” recommends the publishing time most likely to drive engagement, based on audience activity data. “Best posting frequency” is a related but separate question — not when to post, but how many times per day or week to post on a given platform. The two get bundled together in most tools' marketing, but they answer different scheduling questions, which is why both are tracked as distinct rows below.</p><p class="intro">Coverage varies sharply by network. Sprout and Hootsuite support recommendations across the widest set of platforms; Buffer's version is the most restricted, working on Instagram only, and only for professional accounts with 100+ followers and at least 10 posts in the last 7 days.</p>
      
    <div class="table-block">
      
      <div class="table-wrap">
        <table>
          <thead><tr><th>Feature</th><th>Zoho Social</th><th>Buffer</th><th>Sprout Social</th><th>Hootsuite</th></tr></thead>
