      <div class="analysis"><p class="analysis-label">Reading the data</p><p class="analysis-p">Sprout Social and Hootsuite are the only two tools offering best-time-to-post recommendations on every major network tracked here, including LinkedIn and Pinterest, where Zoho Social and Buffer both show “No.” Zoho Social's own coverage skews toward the networks it treats as core — Facebook, Instagram, X, TikTok — but stops short of LinkedIn, Pinterest, and YouTube. On posting frequency specifically, Zoho Social is the only tool with a clear “Yes”; Sprout and Hootsuite don't document a frequency recommendation at all, and Buffer limits it to Instagram.</p><p class="analysis-p">The fallback behavior matters for smaller or newer accounts: Hootsuite and Sprout Social both have a documented plan for what happens when there isn't enough historical engagement data yet — falling back to aggregated research or a content-type sort. Zoho Social and Buffer don't describe an equivalent fallback, which suggests their recommendations may simply not appear until an account has built up enough of its own posting history.</p></div>
      
      
