      <div class="analysis"><p class="analysis-label">Reading the data</p><p class="analysis-p">It's worth reading this table as a warning against assuming “has a free plan” means “has free analytics.” Zoho Social's free tier does not include basic post metrics, despite offering a permanent free plan overall — Buffer is actually the more generous of the two here, giving free users a Sent tab with likes, comments, and impressions for posts published through Buffer, even if it's closer to a publishing log than a real analytics dashboard. Across all four tools, custom reports and audience demographics are locked behind a paid plan with no exceptions, and trial length is the one place Zoho Social is shortest — 15 days, versus 30 for Sprout and Hootsuite.</p></div>
      
      
