    </div>
    
      
      <div class="analysis"><p class="analysis-label">Reading the data</p><p class="analysis-p">The dividing line in this section is native versus routed. Zoho Social's integration with Zoho CRM and Zoho Desk works without a third-party connector, which matters most to a team already inside the Zoho ecosystem — there's no separate app to authorize, map fields for, or maintain. Sprout Social's CRM story is broader in terms of named partners (Salesforce as a preferred partner, plus HubSpot, Zendesk, and Microsoft Dynamics), which makes it the stronger option specifically for teams already standardized on Salesforce. Hootsuite sits in between, with partial coverage across the same interactions via Salesforce or HubSpot rather than a first-party build. Buffer has no CRM integration in this table at all — every row reads “No”.</p></div>
      <div class="callout"><p>“Google Analytics / UTM-based tracking” here means the same thing as Section 06: tagging outgoing social links so GA can attribute traffic to the exact post or campaign. It's listed again in this section because it's part of closing the loop from a CRM record back to the social activity that generated it. All four tools support it — it isn't a differentiator on its own in this comparison.</p></div>
      
