    <section class="section" id="historical">
      <div class="section-head">
        <span class="section-num">14</span>
        <div>
          <p class="kicker">How far back can you look, from the moment you connect a channel</p>
          <h2>Historical data</h2>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p class="intro">This is distinct from data freshness (Section 05), which is about how current live data is. Historical backfill is about what happens the moment you connect a new channel: does the tool pull in your past performance, or does the clock start from zero? The answer determines whether you can run a meaningful before/after or year-over-year comparison the day you switch tools, or whether you have to wait and rebuild that history from scratch.</p><p class="intro">Hootsuite backfills the furthest of the four — data is available from January 1, 2018 across networks, with Instagram audience and Stories backfill included on connect. Buffer offers meaningful backfill at the point of connection too: 6 months of Facebook and LinkedIn channel-level data, 30 days of Instagram posts. Sprout Social supports up to 2 years of Instagram data specifically, but starts every other network from the connection date. Zoho Social's backfill is the narrowest and most time-boxed per network, which means year-over-year comparisons aren't available until an account has accumulated a full year of its own history inside the tool.</p>
      
