      <div class="analysis"><p class="analysis-label">Reading the data</p><p class="analysis-p">X (Twitter) is the network where Zoho Social's backfill window is shortest by its own numbers — a channel metric time range of 0 days, meaning history effectively starts the moment the account is connected, with only up to 100 recent posts pulled in. That's a sharper cutoff than Buffer's equivalent (also up to 100 posts, but explicitly from the last 30 days) and considerably narrower than Hootsuite's full backfill to 2018.</p><p class="analysis-p">The year-over-year comparison row is the clearest practical consequence of all this: Sprout Social and Hootsuite both support it directly, because their backfill or retention windows are long enough to have a prior year on file. Buffer supports it only conditionally, once an account has been active for over a year. Zoho Social doesn't support it at all under current backfill limits — for a content or SEO strategy that leans on year-over-year trend reporting, that's a real planning constraint rather than a minor gap.</p></div>
      
      
