    <section class="section" id="organic-paid">
      <div class="section-head">
        <span class="section-num">15</span>
        <div>
          <p class="kicker">Separate what you earned from what you spent</p>
          <h2>Organic vs paid analytics</h2>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p class="intro">This split matters most on Facebook, Instagram, and LinkedIn — the networks where boosting and sponsored content are part of the strategy. On X, Pinterest, YouTube, TikTok, Google My Business, and Mastodon/Threads/Bluesky, all four tools report organic metrics only, either because there's no paid model on that network or the API doesn't expose paid data — that pattern is consistent enough across every tool that it's really a platform-API constraint, not a tool-by-tool difference.</p>
